# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Environment — copy this file to `.env` and fill it in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env        (macOS / Linux / Git Bash)
#   copy .env.example .env      (Windows CMD)
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env (Windows PowerShell)
#
# `.env` is git-ignored. NEVER commit a key.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Google Maps SDK for Android.
#
# How to get one:
#   1. Open https://console.cloud.google.com/ and create (or pick)
#      a project. Billing must be ENABLED on the project — the Maps
#      SDK for Android requires it — but the free tier covers 28,000
#      map loads a month, so a demo app costs nothing.
#   2. Enable "Maps SDK for Android" under APIs & Services → Library.
#   3. Create an API key under Credentials → Create credentials →
#      API key.
#   4. RESTRICT the key: Android apps → package name
#      `com.codenzic.wayfare` + your signing SHA-1. Do not leave the
#      key unrestricted.
#   5. Paste it below.
#
# Without a key the route screen still builds and runs: the app
# detects that the build has no key and renders the flat-map
# fallback instead of the live Google map. The Maps SDK for Android
# throws a FATAL EXCEPTION with no key, so the app never mounts a
# map it cannot authorise.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Release signing key.
#
# The keystore is a PRIVATE KEY. It is never committed, and neither
# are its passwords — they live here, in `.env`, which is git-ignored.
#
# Generate one with:
#
#   keytool -genkeypair -v -keystore keystores/wayfare-release.keystore \
#     -alias wayfare-release -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000
#
# and then read its fingerprints with:
#
#   keytool -list -v -keystore keystores/wayfare-release.keystore
#
# THE SHA-1 MATTERS
#
# The Google Maps key above is restricted to this app's package name
# plus a signing SHA-1. A release APK signed with a DIFFERENT key has
# a different fingerprint, and the map will render blank tiles on the
# phone. So the release key's SHA-1 has to be added to the Maps key's
# restrictions in the Google Cloud console:
#
#   Credentials → your API key → Application restrictions →
#   Android apps → Add package name + SHA-1 certificate fingerprint
#
# Leave these empty to build with the template's debug signing, which
# is fine for a local run and wrong for an APK that gets installed by
# somebody else.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
WAYFARE_KEYSTORE_PATH=keystores/wayfare-release.keystore
WAYFARE_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD=
WAYFARE_KEY_ALIAS=wayfare-release
WAYFARE_KEY_PASSWORD=
